# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository and on checkout, on
# every platform. Without this, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true by
# default on the GitHub windows-latest runner) rewrites every file to CRLF,
# and `prettier --check .` -- whose .prettierrc.json pins `endOfLine: "lf"`
# -- then flags all ~300 files and fails `verify (windows-latest)`. Keeping
# the normalization here rather than in CI also gives Windows contributors
# the same LF working tree the check expects.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Machine-generated snapshot compared byte-for-byte against a fresh
# regeneration -- the api-contract baseline (.repo-contract, via
# internal-package-contract's own scripts/api-contract/baseline-store.ts,
# still API-Extractor-backed under the hood) emits CRLF unconditionally, so
# git must leave its line endings untouched or every regeneration diff
# breaks. Mirrors this path's existing .prettierignore / eslint ignore
# entries. docs/api-report (TypeDoc + typedoc-plugin-markdown, via
# `npm run docs:api:report`) needs no such override -- TypeDoc's own Markdown
# output is plain Node-written text, never CRLF-emitting.
/.repo-contract/**  -text

# Machine-generated by `npm run docs:api` (TypeDoc), regenerated fresh on
# every CI run, never committed -- see .gitignore/RELEASING.md's "GitHub
# Pages" section. Written entirely by TypeDoc's own Node code (never
# CRLF-emitting), so no -text override is needed here -- just collapse its
# diffs by default in GitHub's own review UI, since a single regeneration can
# touch every page (relevant only if a contributor ever commits a local
# docs/api/ by mistake; .gitignore already excludes it in the normal case).
/docs/api/**  linguist-generated=true
